course: dictionary
lesson: 5506
title: Layout: how things are arranged
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A layout is the way the parts of something are arranged. A town has a layout of streets, a house has a layout of rooms, and a mall has a layout of shops. If you know the layout, you can find things before you look for them.
explain: On a page or screen, layout is the way words and pictures are placed. «An author's choice is a decision about words, sentences or layout, made on purpose.» When a writer decides where a heading or picture goes, that is a choice about layout, not an accident.
explain: Layout can also mean the order of the letters on a keyboard, which is called the keyboard layout. In every case, the layout is the plan that shows where each part belongs.
fact: Layout means the way the parts of something are arranged.
fact: A floor layout shows where the rooms and walls are, like a plan of a house.
fact: A page layout is how the words and pictures are placed on a page or screen.
fact: «Responsive design» makes a page change its layout to fit phones, tablets and laptops.
fact: Layout is a noun. You can have one layout or many layouts.
exercise: «The shop's floor layout puts the toys at the back.» What does layout mean here? | A sign hung over the door | *Hmm | A list of prices | The way the shop's parts are arranged
exercise: Which phrase means the order of the letters on the keys? | *Keyboard layout | Page layout | Floor layout | Layout of the sky
exercise: «CSS sets how pages look; responsive design makes a page change its layout to fit phones, tablets and laptops.» Why would a page change its layout? | To make it longer for no reason | To hide all of its pictures | *To fit phones, tablets and laptops
test: A map of a town shows its layout. What does layout mean in that sentence? | The name of the town | *The way the streets and buildings are arranged | The colour of the map
test: Mia says, «The poster's layout is messy, so nobody reads it.» What is the poster's layout? | Its price | The name of the printer that made it | *The way its words and pictures are arranged
exam: Which best describes a layout? | A type of food | A loud noise from a machine | *The way the parts of something are arranged | A list of words in alphabetical order
